 "relevance_note": "A cohort of 32 children with undifferentiated autoinflammatory disease; Table 3 gives individual-level data for one patient carrying a TNFAIP3 variant: \"| 26 | M | TNFAIP3 {c.1217A>T, p.E406V}\".",
 "method_note": "Read the full paper (no supplementary section; lines after References are references only). Only Table 3 row ID 26 carries a TNFAIP3 variant; the other 31 cohort patients are out of scope (variants in other genes or none) and are counted in cohort_size_as_stated. Label 'Table 3 #26' because Table 3's 'ID' column holds bare numbers. Table 3 columns used: ID, Gender, Results of NGS, Fever, Rash, Serosites, Arthritis, GI, Eye, Hydrocephalus, Sensorineural hearing loss, Laboratory activity, Onset age, Age at the time of diagnosis, Initial treatment (non-biologic), Initial treatment (biologic drugs), Outcome. The table legend defines only abbreviations, not the '+' and '-' symbols, so the '-' cells for this patient (Rash, Serosites, GI, Eye, Hydrocephalus, Sensorineural hearing loss) are recorded as not reported (no excluded rows); '+' cells taken as present. Onset age (5.7) and age at diagnosis (14.7) columns print no unit, so ISO durations are left null. 'Fever' + was not mapped to the checklist item 'recurrent fever' (recurrence not stated for this person; Methods mention persistent fever in some patients), and 'Laboratory activity' + was not mapped to 'elevated inflammatory markers (CRP/ESR)' because the paper does not say which markers it covers for this person. Table 2 'Inheritance' column (AD for TNFAIP3) is the gene's mode of inheritance, not the variant's origin, so inheritance is not reported; no ACMG class is given for the TNFAIP3 variant. Zygosity taken from the named group statement 'Heterozygous genetic variants were found in the remaining 31 patients', which lists TNFAIP3. n_patients_reported=1 is from Table 3 (only row naming TNFAIP3); the authors give no explicit count. The paper also states that all patients had a formal diagnosis of sJIA to qualify for biologic treatment; disease label recorded as uAIDs. Contradictions found: 'no genetic variants were found only in two (6%) patients' yet 'Heterozygous genetic variants were found in the remaining 31 patients' (32-2=30); TREX1 printed as c.914A>G, p.Y305C in Table 2 but c.1079A>G, p.Y360C in Table 3 and text; Pt 4 onset 1.4 in Table 3 vs 'at 1.5 years' in text; corticosteroid share 88% (abstract) vs 85% (results). Built with a short Python script from my own reading; spans checked verbatim by script.",
